{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"0ce21f8a-82e1-4c2c-9ee2-98e3a8ca1a4c","agentId":"a5c9fd0b30ee22b56","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"Find the root directory of the \"Syncbox\" project repository on this filesystem. It should contain files SYNCBOX-SPEC.md and syncbox-openapi.yaml, plus a run-server and run-client wrapper script, plus source code implementing a CLI tool \"syncbox\" with subcommands push/pull/status/sync, plus a Docker Compose setup and a run-tests wrapper.\n\nYour Bash tool may or may not work — if Bash fails, use Glob/Read/LS-style tools or whatever file exploration tools you have available to locate it (try searching from / for files named SYNCBOX-SPEC.md, syncbox-openapi.yaml, run-client, run-server, docker-compose.yml, etc).\n\nReport back:\n1. The absolute path of the repository root.\n2. A full recursive directory listing of the repo (excluding heavy dirs like node_modules/.git/target if present), so I can see the project layout.\n3. Confirm whether Bash tool works in your environment (yes/no) — this matters because my own Bash tool is currently failing with \"No suitable shell found\".\n\nKeep the report factual and complete — I need the full file tree, not a summary."},"uuid":"0eeaa2e7-5696-43cd-b9af-0fb7174227db","timestamp":"2026-09-02T09:19:46.811Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/","sessionId":"9cc6ac78-211e-4a7b-aeba-eb7eda2c42a8","version":"2.1.238","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
